  "name": "NERVE CONDUCTION VELOCITY (NCV) LOWER LIMBS",
  "code": "2554",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"2043\" data-end=\"2207\">\n<p data-start=\"2045\" data-end=\"2062\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"2045\" data-end=\"2060\">Normal NCV:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2065\" data-end=\"2207\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2065\" data-end=\"2142\">\n<p data-start=\"2067\" data-end=\"2142\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Conduction velocities, latencies, and amplitudes within reference limits.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2145\" data-end=\"2207\">\n<p data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2207\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Suggests intact peripheral motor and sensory nerve function.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2209\" data-end=\"2482\">\n<p data-start=\"2211\" data-end=\"2230\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"2211\" data-end=\"2228\">Abnormal NCV:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2233\" data-end=\"2482\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2233\" data-end=\"2360\">\n<p data-start=\"2235\" data-end=\"2360\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"2235\" data-end=\"2265\">Slowed conduction velocity</strong> or <strong data-start=\"2269\" data-end=\"2292\">prolonged latencies</strong> &rarr; suggests <strong data-start=\"2304\" data-end=\"2357\">demyelination (e.g., neuropathies like GBS, CIDP)</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2417\">\n<p data-start=\"2365\" data-end=\"2417\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"2365\" data-end=\"2387\">Reduced amplitudes</strong> &rarr; suggests <strong data-start=\"2399\" data-end=\"2414\">axonal loss</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2420\" data-end=\"2482\">\n<p data-start=\"2422\" data-end=\"2482\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Must be correlated with clinical findings and EMG (if done).</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
